"""
Hard stop on the longitudinal platform: the inherited coast-down driver is swapped for
`Driver.HardStop` by redeclaration, the body is 1500 kg, and a speedometer reads the body speed.

Full throttle (3000 N) for 9 s, coast to 19 s, then full braking (6000 N). At rest the start
acceleration is 3000/1500 = 2 m/s², since drag is zero and rolling resistance is regularized to
zero at standstill. The car reaches 6.62 m/s at 21 s, still moving, so the ideal brake force
has not yet reversed it; the coast-down driver the platform defaults to would still be near 14 m/s.
"""
test component HardStop
  extends VehicleComponents.Examples.Platforms.Longitudinal(driver = VehicleComponents.Driver.HardStop(), body(m = 1500.0))
  speedometer = TranslationalComponents.Sensors.VelocitySensor() {^speedometer}
relations
  connect(body.flange, speedometer.flange) {^w8}
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "tests": {
      "hard_stop": {
        "stop": 21,
        "solver": "Auto",
        "abstol": 1e-6,
        "reltol": 1e-6,
        "atol": {"body.mass.a": 0.001, "speedometer.v": 0.001},
        "expect": {
          "initial": {"body.mass.a": 2.0, "speedometer.v": 0},
          "final": {"speedometer.v": 6.6229077},
          "signals": ["speedometer.v", "body.mass.a"]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "_links": {
    "speedometer": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 1200, "x2": 1300, "y1": 280, "y2": 380}}}},
    "w8": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}}
  }
}
end
